# What building the timetable needs. Copy this to builder/.env and fill it in; `uv run
# ir-build-data` reads it there (or a .env here, at the repository root), and a variable set in
# the environment wins over both. The Deploy workflow takes it from a GitHub secret instead.

# Required: a free token from https://511.org/open-data/token. The builder downloads the Bay
# Area's transit schedules (511.org's regional feed for every operator) with it. It is never
# printed, and stays out of what the site serves.
API_511_KEY=

# --- Walk and bike routing ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not read from here. VITE_ROUTING_PROVIDER and VITE_VALHALLA_ROUTE_URL are settings for building
# the site, from the environment or frontend/.env (DEPLOY.md). The default, the public Valhalla
# server, needs neither, and no key.
